	"department": "MUSIC",
	"description": [
		"This course delves into the unique history of Musical Theatre in Japan. Students explore Japanese theatrical traditions and observe their influence on contemporary productions and pop culture. Activities include performances of Noh, Kabuki, Takarazuka, translated American musicals, Disneyland, and original Japanese musicals. Guest lectures from industry professionals provide insights into training, career trajectory, and considerations for translation. The course culminates in reflections on the role of musical theater in society, both locally and globally. Offered alternate years during January term."
	],
